                              UN/EDIFACT

                      Draft directory for test purposes

       This is not a UNECE publication. It is a hand written sample that
       exercises three defects in the batch message conversion: an element
       name that is not a legal identifier, a segment repeated inside one
       segment group, and a reference to a service segment that the standard
       segments directory does not define.

4.3    Message structure

4.3.1  Segment table

Pos    Tag Name                                      S   R

           HEADER SECTION

0010   UNH Message header                            M   1
0020   BGM Beginning of message                      M   1
0030   DGS Dangerous goods                           C   9

0040       ----- Segment group 1  ------------------ C   5-----------+
0050   RFF Reference                                 M   1           |
0060   FTX Free text                                 C   5           |
0070   TAX Duty/tax/fee details                      C   5           |
0080   FTX Free text                                 C   9-----------+

0090       ----- Segment group 2  ------------------ C   9-----------+
0100   UGH Anti-collision segment group header       M   1           |
0110   NAD Name and address                          C   9           |
0120   UGT Anti-collision segment group trailer      M   1-----------+

0130   UNT Message trailer                           M   1
